Support project specific extensions configuration with 'extensions.json' file in the '.vscode' or a '.project' folder to control the vscode to install/enable the required extensions specific to the project.

The configuration file 'extensions.json' may looks like the following example:
{
 "Prettier":{
 "version":"^1.0.0",
 "enable":true
 }
}

The configuration will instruct vscode to install the required extensions and enable or disable extensions configured in the 'extensions.json' file.

Hello;
More often than not, you're in a situation where you want to have a specific tab locked to the side si that you don't end up closing it by mistake.
It would be cool if we could lock every opened tab all at once, or lock them separately. It would also be great if VSCode prompts you with an alert message when you try to close a locked tab.
